        "Natural convection is driven by buoyancy: heated fluid expands, loses density and rises, setting a gentle circulation measured by the Grashof number. Forced convection is driven by a fan or pump and scales with the Reynolds number. A Nigerian plant with unreliable fans sees the difference directly: forced-draft coolers collapse to natural convection duty within seconds of a power trip, a {S} reality in equipment ratings.",
