        "Feed a column with 100 kmol/h containing 40 percent benzene; distillate is 90 percent benzene and bottoms 5 percent. Total balance with D plus B = 100, and benzene balance 0.40 x 100 = 0.90 D + 0.05 B gives D = 35/0.85 = 41.2 kmol/h and B = 58.8 kmol/h. Every {S} column design opens with exactly these two equations.",
        "For a binary with relative volatility 2.5 and liquid mole fraction 0.2, the equilibrium vapour fraction is y = alpha x / (1 + (alpha - 1) x) = 0.5/1.3 = 0.385. The vapour is nearly twice as rich in light component as the liquid, which is the leverage {S} distillation repeats stage by stage.",
